/-!
# Radical bounds in the surviving component cases

Both original radical bounds are proved for all three surviving alternatives.
In the SL₂ odd-extension branch, the canonical A.3.6 full-core actions have
solvable seed kernels and two-dimensional Frattini quotients. The scalar
calculation and Burnside kernel prove centralization of the whole Fitting
subgroup, retaining higher exponents. Its controlled centralizer detects
O₂ in the local overgroup KR₁X; the literal quotient and core identities
return [R₁,X] ≤ O₂(KT). The SL₂ quotient itself supplies noncentrality.
No action of the full simple ambient group is assumed.

Triangle exclusion and the surviving bounds now give the full (2–3) output
on the unchanged chosen flag. The parent component assembly discharges the
registered earlier inputs. The independent Fitting-index bound remains
conditional: the existing exact formula reduces it to R₁ ≤ K O₂(KT).
The canonical commutator proof completes the required source output without
that stronger intermediate result; the conditional index APIs are preserved.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, original 11.4.1(3), printed pp.775--776.
-/
